    "subtitle": "A guest joins the group · 1",
    "context": "Use the selected vocabulary and constructions to welcome someone, establish relationships and resolve a misunderstanding about who is involved.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U6-01-skill-K-HSK6-listen-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "HSK 6: listen",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Compare accounts at the level of claims and qualifications. Identify shared ground, the exact disagreement and what neither speaker has established; do not resolve uncertainty by guessing.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "互助",
                "pinyin": "hùzhù",
                "meaning": "to help each other",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "2ee30e6bfbeb52df3543eee30b3ce144f46349f5135ea2c28895a2704ccfef6e"
              },
              {
                "text": "诚信",
                "pinyin": "chéngxìn",
                "meaning": "honesty; trustworthiness",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "84c699b5217473c1bdc71dd0ad00baacca4194401d832e656d800fb86c7fad64"
              },
              {
                "text": "可能",
                "pinyin": "kěnéng",
                "meaning": "might; possible",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "64e53487039dd8101be9ee0d489e64544cd5b06f7f1b9e6255cca2a09f76149c"
              },
              {
                "text": "认为",
                "pinyin": "rènwéi",
                "meaning": "to believe; to think",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "cb6fec095e11769414fd90d687de1cd4adc5a3c7f78407502416584a9885e0a5"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A and B discuss a social situation. The first two clauses are A’s; the last two are B’s.\nFamiliar meanings available: to help each other; honesty; trustworthiness; might; possible; to believe; to think."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
